ummary", "oldValue": "Vincent Michael Conçessao is a prominent Indian Catholic clergyman who was installed as the fifth Archbishop of Delhi in November 2000. He served as Vice President of the Catholic Bishops' Conference of India from 2000 to 2004.", "newValue": "Vincent Michael Conçessao, born on September 28, 1936, in Mangaluru, India, emerged as a pivotal figure in the Indian Catholic Church, culminating in his installation as the fifth Archbishop of Delhi in November 2000. His ecclesiastical career spanned significant periods of social and political change in India, positioning him as a vocal advocate for interfaith dialogue, educational development, and social justice within a rapidly modernizing nation. His leadership in the archdiocese and national episcopal bodies underscored the Catholic Church's evolving role in post-colonial India, emphasizing community building and engagement with secular governance.

